      "text": [
        " : سَأَلْتُ أَبَا اَلْحَسَنِ مُوسَى بْنَ جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِمَا اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنْ شَيْءٍ فَقَالَ لِي \"كُلُّ مَجْهُولٍ فَفِيهِ اَلْقُرْعَةُ\" فَقُلْتُ إِنَّ اَلْقُرْعَةَ تُخْطِئُ وَ تُصِيبُ فَقَالَ \"كُلُّ مَا حَكَمَ اَللَّهُ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ بِهِ فَلَيْسَ بِمُخْطِئٍ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3389 - Narrated by Muhammad ibn al-Hakim:\n\"I asked Abu al-Hasan Imam Musa ibn Jafar Al-Kadhim (as) about a matter.\nImam (as) said to me: 'For every unknown matter, the solution lies in casting lots (Qur'ah).'\nI said: 'But casting lots can be right or wrong.'\nImam (as) replied: 'Whatever Allah (swt), the Mighty and Majestic, decrees is never wrong.'\""
        ]
      }
